  "coverage": [
    "Strict v1/v2 plain own-data validation, per-step and cross-step eight-target budget, duplicate rejection, final release, deep detachment and freezing.",
    "Immutable range editing, whole/instance clearing and explicit lossless v1-to-v2 conversion; existing v2 clones retain all original targets.",
    "Frozen controlled physical target identity and actor order, including two instances with one OC objectId.",
    "Actual HTTP route plus createProjectBuildService and direct runProjectBuild: unknown/static/sensor/nonphysical/controls=none targets are refused for plain replay and embedded case.program before task ID change, native phases, session directories or author/frozen-build writes.",
    "Missing instance capability is refused for both HTTP and direct Node-host entry while legacy discovery stays available.",
    "Frozen target directory remains authoritative after the live author scene changes. A deliberately failed injected run phase demonstrates admission only, not physical execution or gameplay correctness.",
    "Same-OC two-instance replay and acceptance save/update/reload with exact BOM/CRLF input bytes; unknown author-scene targets reject create/update before writes.",
    "Selective resource export includes scene, physics, shared OC definitions and referenced images; migrated definitions reload while the original workspace is offline.",
    "Stale input targets block author export independently of valid acceptance checks. Both ordinary replay and embedded acceptance payloads forged into checksum-correct ZIP archives are rejected by the package reader.",
    "Existing v1 author-save, source-version conflict and resource-migration regressions remain enabled."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "The controlled host registry uses real capture/generation and frozen-record admission but injects identify/executePhase; no Godot process or host-side physics simulation occurs in these tests.",
    "HTTP uses a real loopback server and the production handleApiRequest router wired to the actual project build service, not a complete packaged application server.",
    "Direct Node-host API runProjectBuild is covered. The shell CLI currently has no physics replay/case flags and is not claimed supported.",
    "Pure-model first exploratory failure was an invalid reordered source-map test fixture; its console output was not saved as an original log. This archive contains the available original final pure log and all saved host iteration logs without reconstructing missing raw output.",
    "Native movement, jump edges, solver behavior, browser interaction and full application checks require their separately scoped evidence."
  ]
